        qa("What's the difference between `==` and `is`?",
           "`==` compares values by calling `__eq__`; `is` checks whether two names refer to the very same object. Use `is` only for singletons such as None, True and False.",
           "Code reviews flag `if x == None`; write `if x is None`. Comparing strings or numbers with `is` can appear to work because of caching, then fail for other values."),
