        qa("Explain the mutable default argument problem.",
           "Default values are evaluated once, when the function is defined, not on each call. A default list or dict is therefore shared between calls, so changes leak from one call into the next. Default to None and create a fresh object inside the function.",
           "It's one of the most common Python bugs in production code, and linters such as ruff (rule B006) flag it automatically."),
